  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Muhammed Fazil K. A vs Thiruvananthapuram Corporation on 7 February, 2025 2025:Ker:10291 Wp(C) No. 3111 Of 2025 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice Ziyad Rahman A.A. Friday, The 7Th Day Of February 2025 / 18Th Magha, 1946 Wp(C) No. 3111 Of 2025 Petitioner: Muhammed Fazil K. A., Aged 38 Years, Proprietor, Spicy Kitchen, T.C. 29/3384, Dpi Road, Vazhuthacaud, Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695014 By Advs. Enoch David Simon Joel S.Sreedev Rony Jose Leo Lukose Karol Mathews Sebastian Alencherry Derick Mathai Saji Karan Scaria Abraham Ittoop Joy Thattil Respondents: 1 Thiruvananthapuram Corporation Vikas Bhavan P.O, Thiruvananthapuram Represented By Its Secretary, Pin - 695033 2 Secretary Thiruvananthapuram Corporation, Vikas Bhavan P.O, Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695033 2025:Ker:10291 Wp(C) No. 3111 Of 2025 2 Muhammed Fazil K. A vs Thiruvananthapuram Corporation on 7 February, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/7429644/ 1 3 Health Inspector, Thiruvananthapuram Corporation, Vikas Bhavan P.O, Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695033 4 Dr. Prathapachandran Nair, Sri. Vidhyadhiraja Dental Clinic, T.C. 29/3381, Dpi Road, Vazhuthacaud, Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695014 By Adv Sri.Suman Chakravarthy, Sc This Writ Petition (Civil) Having Come Up For Admission On 07.02.2025, The Court On The Same Day Delivered The Following: 2025:Ker:10291 Wp(C) No. 3111 Of 2025 3 Judgment",
    "facts": "The petitioner is aggrieved by Ext.P7 order issued by the 2nd respondent, by which the restaurant run by the petitioner was ordered to be closed. Being aggrieved by the same, the petitioner submitted a statutory appeal, before the Corporation Council as evidenced by Ext.P9 on the next day itself.",
